\refcardt{Definition}{Overlong reward shaping}{Section 3.4}{yu2025dapo}{
\p{Overlong reward shaping introduces a soft penalty near the maximum response
length before the hard truncation boundary. The penalty increases over a
declared buffer region rather than assigning the same abrupt terminal penalty
to every response that reaches the limit.}

\p{The construction changes both the reward value and which length-related
behavior receives gradient. The maximum length, buffer width, and penalty
schedule are part of the reward design.}
}
